  "notes": "Rework for DEF-016 (DR-MOD-031-2). Cause: the seven MOD-027/MOD-028 Developer unit tests named in the defect still seeded Layercake.silv_daily_count_detail and Layercake.fact_daily_member_count_detail at the pre-MOD-031 grain, so the gold load's #det_stage rejected the NULL local_group_id. Fix (test-only, as docs/answers.md 'MOD-031 regression: older tests at the old grain' allows): in tests/tsqlt/test_MOD027_dev.sql (3 tests) and tests/tsqlt/test_MOD028_dev.sql (4 tests) the seeded silver rows now also carry local_group_id 0, contact_country_id = country_id and contact_region = region, and the seeded fact rows carry local_group_id 0 and contact_country_id = country_id. Test names, data, expectations and the other tests in both files are unchanged. No SetUp change was needed: the gold load's left join to Layercake.silv_ref_local_group finds the seeded row 0 not reportable (is_reportable 0), so country_id stays the silver one. No MOD-031 object changed. run_tests: 40 passed, 0 failed. Round-trip of MIG-0033 passes and check passes.\n\nRework after DR-MOD-031-2 (DEF-016). Test-first: the first run had 21 of 21 of the Tester's tests passing; the final run passed 21 of 21 and 8 unit test(s), in 2 run(s)."
